            <ArticleTitle>Stereoselective and Catalytic Synthesis of anti-β-Alkoxy-α-azido Carboxylic Derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6400-6403</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03255</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Direct addition of a chiral N-azidoacetyl thiazolidinethione to a variety of dialkyl acetals catalyzed by a commercially available and structurally simple nickel(II) complex gives access in good yields and a highly stereocontrolled manner to anti-β-alkoxy-α-azido carboxylic derivatives which, in turn, can be easily converted into a wide array of enantiomerically pure compounds.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
